{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734802",
      "title": "Data Fetching via loader()s",
      "sourceHash": "b9a14df51c6b52a9261960d3ce9c4b0c6d7f40f596cd72e8ba0cf52956e16445",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 3.9,
          "en": "Now with routing added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.9,
          "end": 7.68,
          "en": "we added another crucial feature to this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.68,
          "end": 9.6,
          "en": "a feature which is especially important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.6,
          "end": 12,
          "en": "in more complex web applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12,
          "end": 13.47,
          "en": "you might be building with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.47,
          "end": 18.47,
          "en": "And React router, at least if you have version 6.4",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.11,
          "end": 23.4,
          "en": "or higher installed, also offers some amazing features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 26.16,
          "en": "that go beyond picking the right component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.16,
          "end": 27.93,
          "en": "for the right path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.93,
          "end": 31.59,
          "en": "Instead, React router, when using version 6.4 or higher",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.59,
          "end": 34.74,
          "en": "also helps with data fetching and data submission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.74,
          "end": 37.65,
          "en": "And that's now the last part we're also going to explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.65,
          "end": 38.913,
          "en": "in this crash course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.87,
          "end": 42.42,
          "en": "Because of course here we are fetching data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.42,
          "end": 45.87,
          "en": "in the Posts component, we have the PostsList component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.87,
          "end": 49.32,
          "en": "and in there, we are fetching data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.32,
          "end": 51.63,
          "en": "We have this useEffect hook here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.63,
          "end": 55.02,
          "en": "where we load our posts and set our posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.02,
          "end": 58.23,
          "en": "We also have to code for sending postData here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.23,
          "end": 60.78,
          "en": "but that code isn't used at the moment anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.78,
          "end": 62.38,
          "en": "and I'll get back to that later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.39,
          "end": 65.04,
          "en": "But when it comes to fetching data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 67.56,
          "en": "we could stick to useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.56,
          "end": 70.53,
          "en": "But when using React router version 6.4 or higher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.53,
          "end": 73.17,
          "en": "we have a more convenient way of doing so.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.17,
          "end": 75.15,
          "en": "Because with that version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.15,
          "end": 77.31,
          "en": "you can go to your route definitions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.31,
          "end": 79.08,
          "en": "to the route that needs data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.08,
          "end": 81.53999999999999,
          "en": "so the Posts route here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.53999999999999,
          "end": 85.623,
          "en": "and you can add a loader property to that route definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.58,
          "end": 88.11,
          "en": "Now the loader property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.11,
          "end": 91.44,
          "en": "expects to get a function as a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.44,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "and React router will execute that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 97.05,
          "en": "whenever that route gets activated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.05,
          "end": 100.17,
          "en": "so whenever it's about to render this element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.17,
          "end": 102.57,
          "en": "That's when this function gets executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.57,
          "end": 105.15,
          "en": "and you can therefore use this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.15,
          "end": 109.2,
          "en": "to load and prepare any data that might be needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.2,
          "end": 110.94,
          "en": "by this route component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.94,
          "end": 114.24000000000001,
          "en": "or any other component used as part of that route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.24000000000001,
          "end": 115.97999999999999,
          "en": "so any nested component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.97999999999999,
          "end": 118.803,
          "en": "used inside of the Posts component, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.63,
          "end": 123.57,
          "en": "Now therefore, we could add the data fetching logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.57,
          "end": 126.75,
          "en": "for sending that HTTP request here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.75,
          "end": 129.81,
          "en": "But to keep this main JSX file lean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.81,
          "end": 133.17,
          "en": "it's more common to go to your route component file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.17,
          "end": 136.02,
          "en": "so in this case, the Posts.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.02,
          "end": 139.53,
          "en": "and there, export an extra function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.53,
          "end": 141.24,
          "en": "which typically is called loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.24,
          "end": 143.49,
          "en": "though the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 143.49,
          "end": 145.14,
          "en": "But loader is a common convention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 145.14,
          "end": 147.06,
          "en": "since this will be the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147.06,
          "end": 149.76,
          "en": "that will be assigned to that loader property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 149.76,
          "end": 151.143,
          "en": "in the route definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 151.98,
          "end": 153.69,
          "en": "Now that loader function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 153.69,
          "end": 155.79,
          "en": "still executes on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 155.79,
          "end": 158.64,
          "en": "It's still code that executes in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 158.64,
          "end": 161.55,
          "en": "And therefore, in there, you can do whatever you wanna do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 161.55,
          "end": 165,
          "en": "that could be done anywhere else in this app as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 165,
          "end": 166.54,
          "en": "Here I wanna fetch my posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 166.54,
          "end": 170.19,
          "en": "And therefore, I'll go to the PostsList component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 170.19,
          "end": 174,
          "en": "and copy these two lines of code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 174,
          "end": 177,
          "en": "The state updating code does not matter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 177,
          "end": 178.68,
          "en": "because this loader function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 178.68,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "executes outside of the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 183.87,
          "en": "and can't manipulate component state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 183.87,
          "end": 186.51,
          "en": "You will still see how we then get the posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 186.51,
          "end": 188.673,
          "en": "into the component a little bit later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 189.69,
          "end": 192.54,
          "en": "So I cut the code for fetching data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 192.54,
          "end": 194.52,
          "en": "and back in Posts.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 194.52,
          "end": 196.593,
          "en": "I'll paste it into this loader function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 197.49,
          "end": 199.53,
          "en": "Now since I used the await keyword here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 199.53,
          "end": 200.91,
          "en": "we should add async",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 200.91,
          "end": 203.91,
          "en": "in front of that function to unlock that keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 203.91,
          "end": 205.26,
          "en": "and we can't do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 205.26,
          "end": 208.05,
          "en": "because this function which will be assigned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 208.05,
          "end": 211.17000000000002,
          "en": "to this loader property can be an async",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 211.17000000000002,
          "end": 212.88,
          "en": "or a synchronous function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 212.88,
          "end": 215.52,
          "en": "It may return a promise or it may not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 215.52,
          "end": 218.19,
          "en": "React router does not care about it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 218.19,
          "end": 220.23,
          "en": "But if it does return a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 220.23,
          "end": 223.8,
          "en": "React router will wait for that promise to resolve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 223.8,
          "end": 227.37,
          "en": "before it then renders this route component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 227.37,
          "end": 229.623,
          "en": "so this element which you specified here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 230.49,
          "end": 232.68,
          "en": "And therefore here we can use async",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 232.68,
          "end": 236.25,
          "en": "and then send our request to fetch all posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 236.25,
          "end": 238.26,
          "en": "and extract the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 238.26,
          "end": 240.66,
          "en": "And then, that's the important part,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 240.66,
          "end": 243.9,
          "en": "we can return the data that we wanna expose",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 243.9,
          "end": 247.323,
          "en": "to the element that is rendered for the active route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 248.61,
          "end": 251.31,
          "en": "So in this case, resData.posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 251.31,
          "end": 254.67,
          "en": "I return that as part of this loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 254.67,
          "end": 259.05,
          "en": "And then in main.jsx, we can import this loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 259.05,
          "end": 262.17,
          "en": "by editing this import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 262.17,
          "end": 265.32,
          "en": "where we import the posts component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 265.32,
          "end": 268.35,
          "en": "And there, we can also import this loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 268.35,
          "end": 269.94,
          "en": "and I'll give it an alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 269.94,
          "end": 273.3,
          "en": "since we might have more loaders from different routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 273.3,
          "end": 276,
          "en": "and we don't wanna have name clashes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 276,
          "end": 277.71,
          "en": "We could name this postsLoader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 280.05,
          "en": "but of course this name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 280.05,
          "end": 282.72,
          "en": "So in the end, it's now this loader function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 282.72,
          "end": 284.55,
          "en": "which is assigned as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 284.55,
          "end": 287.67,
          "en": "for this loader property in this route definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 287.67,
          "end": 291,
          "en": "And therefore, React router will execute this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 291,
          "end": 293.34000000000003,
          "en": "and wait for the promise to resolve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 293.34000000000003,
          "end": 295.803,
          "en": "before it then renders this element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 297.03,
          "end": 299.64,
          "en": "And the data we return here in this loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 299.64,
          "end": 302.61,
          "en": "is actually exposed to this element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 302.61,
          "end": 305.91,
          "en": "React router will make sure that the data returned here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 305.91,
          "end": 308.4,
          "en": "can be accessed in this route element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 308.4,
          "end": 310.77,
          "en": "or in any nested component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 310.77,
          "end": 313.413,
          "en": "so also in postsList, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 314.31,
          "end": 316.86,
          "en": "that's what we can go to postsList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 316.86,
          "end": 319.29,
          "en": "And there, we can now import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 319.29,
          "end": 322.98,
          "en": "and never hook from react-router-dom,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 322.98,
          "end": 327.21,
          "en": "and that would be the useLoaderData hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 328.587,
          "end": 330.3,
          "en": "Now this hook can be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 330.3,
          "end": 331.92,
          "en": "inside of the component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 331.92,
          "end": 334.29,
          "en": "Like all Hooks, it must only be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 334.29,
          "end": 336.81,
          "en": "inside of component functions in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 336.81,
          "end": 339.96,
          "en": "and that gives us the data that is returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 339.96,
          "end": 343.17,
          "en": "by this loader that's assigned to this route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 343.17,
          "end": 344.97,
          "en": "which is the route that is active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 344.97,
          "end": 347.73,
          "en": "when the postsList component is rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 347.73,
          "end": 350.19,
          "en": "So here I get my posts in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 350.19,
          "end": 354.09000000000003,
          "en": "because in my loader here, I'm returning the posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 354.09000000000003,
          "end": 357.3,
          "en": "So that's what I get here with help of use loader data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 357.3,
          "end": 360.63,
          "en": "Therefore, we can get rid of that posts state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 360.63,
          "end": 363.33,
          "en": "We can also get rid of the IsFetching state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 363.33,
          "end": 366.36,
          "en": "because the loading state of this route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 366.36,
          "end": 370.35,
          "en": "and this route component will be handled differently soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 370.35,
          "end": 373.71,
          "en": "And we can also get rid of this entire useEffect call here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 373.71,
          "end": 377.13,
          "en": "because we don't useEffect for data fetching anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 377.13,
          "end": 380.88,
          "en": "Instead, we use this feature provided by React router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 380.88,
          "end": 383.37,
          "en": "We therefore should also remove these imports",
